    "en-gdpr-erasure": {
      "answer": "A data subject has the right to have personal data erased when the data are no longer necessary for the purposes they were collected or processed [1], or when the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal basis for processing [1], or when the data subject objects to processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds [1], or when the data were unlawfully processed [1], or for compliance with a legal obligation [1], or when the data were collected in relation to information society services [1].",
