    "adv-no-citations": {
      "answer": "An AI system is considered high-risk when it poses a significant risk of harm to health, safety, or fundamental rights [2]. This applies to systems used in predefined high-risk areas, unless specific derogations apply, such as performing narrow procedural tasks or improving previously completed human activities [2]. Additionally, AI systems that perform profiling of natural persons are always considered high-risk [2].",
