    "tool-compare": {
      "answer": "The notification of a personal data breach under GDPR Article 33 requires reporting within 72 hours, unless the risk is low, and includes specific details about the breach [6, 8]. In contrast, the AI Act's Article 73 mandates reporting of serious incidents immediately after establishing a causal link or within 15 days, with exceptions for deaths or widespread infringements requiring reporting within 10 or 2 days [1, 5, 11]. Both require cooperation with authorities and documentation [6, 10, 12].",
